# Build context exclusions for the shado-cloud image.
#
# Docker does NOT honour .gitignore, so without this file `COPY . .` bakes in real secrets
# and the full git history. Everything below was previously ending up inside the image.

# ── Secrets. config.yml holds cross-service.secret, the DB and Redis passwords, the
# password vault salt, the GitHub webhook secret and Google OAuth credentials. Image layers
# are immutable and readable by anyone who can pull, so a secret baked in once is disclosed
# for the life of every tag that contains it. Config is mounted at runtime instead.
config.yml
.env
.env.*
!.example.env
*.pem
*.key

# ── Git history: 30MB and 611 commits, including anything ever committed and later removed.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ── Installed inside the image by `npm install`; copying the host's copy in as well doubles
# the image size, and at runtime it is shadowed by a volume anyway. Host-built native modules
# (node-pty) may also be compiled for the wrong platform.
node_modules

# ── Build output, regenerated by `nest build` in the image.
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Never needed at runtime.
test
coverage
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
README.md

# Throwaway smoke-test config; never part of an image.
.smoke-config.yml
